    {
      "text": "Central and L p -concentration of 1-Lipschitz maps into R -trees — In this paper, we study the Le´vy-Milman concentration phenomenon of 1-Lipschitz maps from mm-spaces to R-trees.\n\n**Central and L p -concentration of 1-Lipschitz maps into R -trees**\n\n*By Kei FUNANO*\n\n24 pp, 14 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** In this paper, we study the Le´vy-Milman concentration phenomenon of 1-Lipschitz maps from mm-spaces to R-trees. Our main theorems assert that the concentration to R-trees is equivalent to the concentration to the real line.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction.; 2 Preliminaries.; 2.1 Basics of the concentration and the Lp-con; 2.1.1 Observable diameter and separation dista; 2.1.2 Observable Lp-variation.; 2.2 Basics of R-trees.; 2.3 Center of mass of a measure on a CAT(0)-sp; 2.3.1 Basics of the center of mass of a measur; 2.3.2 Observable central radius.; 3 Existence of a median in an R-tree.; 4 The necessity in Proposition 2.12 for R-tree; 5 Proof of the main theorems.; References",
